Description: fate/hevc: test an asymmetric layer inclusion mask
 Add a two-view sample with layer IDs 0 and 6 and vps_max_layer_id 7.
 The added layer_id_included_flag[1][7] is zero, so the layer set and
 coded pictures are unchanged from mv_nuh_layer_id.bit. Use that
 sample's existing reference to check both views.
 .
 The flags are not palindromic, exposing the reversed bit order of the
 old get_bits64() reader. The test fails on unpatched master with both
 one and four decoder threads.
 .
 Generate the sample with make-hevc-vps-max-layer-id.py from the
 accompanying sample request. Install it in hevc/mv-vps-max-layer-id.hevc
 in the FATE sample suite.
 .
